
"smart_sources:2026-05-20 - A Windfall Profits Tax Is a Way to Drill Less and Raise Consumer Costs.md": {"path":"2026-05-20 - A Windfall Profits Tax Is a Way to Drill Less and Raise Consumer Costs.md","last_embed":{"hash":null},"embeddings":{},"last_read":{"hash":"wj9cku","at":1785795032780},"class_name":"SmartSource","last_import":{"mtime":1783545937562,"size":6301,"at":1785795032968,"hash":"wj9cku"},"blocks":{"#---frontmatter---":[1,9],"#":[10,37],"##{1}":[24,24],"##{2}":[25,25],"##{3}":[26,26],"##{4}":[27,37]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Thomas Aiello","target":"Thomas Aiello","line":5},{"title":"wrote","target":"https://www.ntu.org/publications/detail/imposing-a-new-tax-on-energy-producers-will-not-lower-gas-prices","line":12},{"title":"Congressional Research Service notes","target":"https://www.everycrsreport.com/reports/RL33305.html","line":22}],"metadata":{"title":"A Windfall Profits Tax Is a Way to Drill Less and Raise Consumer Costs","source":"https://www.ntu.org/publications/detail/a-windfall-profits-tax-is-a-way-to-drill-less-and-raise-consumer-costs","author":["[[Thomas Aiello]]"],"published":"2026-05-20","created":"2026-07-08","description":"Consumers nationwide are feeling a pinch due to surging energy prices. After reaching a five-year low earlier this year, prices are now approaching a five-year high. It’s no surprise this price whiplash has attracted the attention of policymakers in Washington. Yet, rather than real solutions—such as permitting reform or further regulatory changes—some Democrats are once again pushing a policy idea that should have stayed buried decades ago: a “windfall profits” tax. Like every bad idea in Washi, Author(s): Thomas Aiello"},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[]},